From 35bbecf216720cc2d46a7ee3caf4037ac9d5650b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yiyu Zhou <yiyu@yiyuzhou.io>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 07:31:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 37/47] workflows: update the openwrt image builder before the
 check

packages.x86_64-linux.openwrt imports package lists that the OpenWrt
Image Builder fetches with pinned hashes, which go stale whenever
OpenWrt rebuilds its package indexes, and which the Image Builder
updates once a day.  On November 28, the index of mips_24kc failed with
a hash mismatch with the lock of November 26, so the check would have
failed on nearly every run for a reason that no commit here can fix for
long.

Update the openwrt-imagebuilder input before the check, as building the
image needs anyway, and keep every other input as flake.lock pins it.
The update takes the newest Image Builder code and its own flake-parts,
nixpkgs and systems inputs as well, not only its hashes, so the check
no longer tests that input as committed, and two runs of one commit can
differ.  The run does not commit the updated lock.

This narrows the gap but does not close it: the Image Builder of
November 27 evaluated at 10:52 UTC on November 28 and failed at 15:35
UTC, after OpenWrt had rebuilt the index again, and runs in such a
window fail until the Image Builder updates its hashes.
---
 .github/workflows/check.yml | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/check.yml b/.github/workflows/check.yml
index 9716669..930ac56 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/check.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/check.yml
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
-# Runs `nix flake check` with the inputs that flake.lock pins, on each
-# push and pull request.  It evaluates every NixOS and nix-darwin
-# configuration and package, and checks the formatting, in a few
-# minutes, without building any system.
+# Runs `nix flake check` on each push and pull request, with the inputs
+# that flake.lock pins, except openwrt-imagebuilder, which it updates
+# first.  It evaluates every NixOS and nix-darwin configuration and
+# package, and checks the formatting, in a few minutes, without building
+# any system.
 name: check
 on:
   push:
@@ -21,6 +22,19 @@ jobs:
             # Substitute from the caches that the nixConfig of flake.nix names
             accept-flake-config = true
 
+      # The OpenWrt Image Builder pins the hashes of the package indexes
+      # of OpenWrt, which change whenever OpenWrt rebuilds packages, and
+      # updates them once a day, so packages.x86_64-linux.openwrt soon
+      # fails to evaluate with an older lock.  The update takes the newest
+      # Image Builder code and its own inputs as well, not only the
+      # hashes, so the check does not test that input as committed, and
+      # two runs of one commit can differ.  Building the image needs this
+      # update anyway; the run does not commit it.  The check can still
+      # fail on the OpenWrt package between a rebuild of OpenWrt and the
+      # next update of the Image Builder.
+      - name: Update the OpenWrt Image Builder
+        run: nix flake update openwrt-imagebuilder
+
       # --all-systems evaluates the checks of aarch64-darwin, which are
       # the nix-darwin configurations.
       - name: Check the flake
-- 
